---
title: "withdrawExcessInvestedCapital (LegionPreLiquidOpenApplicationSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_pause: investor calls withdrawExcessInvestedCapital(acceptedAmount, merkleProof)
    q_check_pause --> q_error_paused: contract is paused
    q_error_paused --> [*]: revert Paused
    q_check_pause --> q_check_root: contract not paused
    q_check_root --> q_error_root: acceptedCapitalMerkleRoot == bytes32(0)
    q_error_root --> [*]: revert AcceptedCapitalNotSet
    q_check_root --> q_check_claimed: acceptedCapitalMerkleRoot != bytes32(0)
    q_check_claimed --> q_error_claimed: position.excessClaimed == true
    q_error_claimed --> [*]: revert ExcessAlreadyClaimed
    q_check_claimed --> q_verify_proof: position.excessClaimed == false
    q_verify_proof --> q_error_proof: MerkleProof.verify(proof, root, leaf(investor, acceptedAmount)) == false
    q_error_proof --> [*]: revert InvalidMerkleProof
    q_verify_proof --> q_calc_excess: proof valid
    q_calc_excess --> q_check_excess: excessAmount = position.investedCapital - acceptedAmount
    q_check_excess --> q_error_no_excess: excessAmount == 0
    q_error_no_excess --> [*]: revert NoExcessCapital
    q_check_excess --> q_transfer: excessAmount > 0
    q_transfer --> q_update: transfer excessAmount of bidToken to investor
    q_update --> q_emit: position.excessClaimed = true
    q_emit --> [*]: emit ExcessCapitalWithdrawn(investor, excessAmount)

    note right of q_verify_proof
        INV-001: Excess withdrawal uses Merkle proof to verify accepted allocation
        INV-002: excessAmount = investedCapital - acceptedAmount (no underflow)
        INV-003: Each investor can claim excess exactly once (excessClaimed flag)
        INV-004: acceptedAmount <= position.investedCapital for valid proofs
    end note
